   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilience and strengthening agricultural value chains for economic transformation in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Small holder farmers in Sudan and in Africa in general face challenges associated with erratic rainfall patterns, prolonged droughts and the worsening impacts of climate change that cast greater uncertainty on food availability. In Sudan this has been made worse by armed conflict.  A study by the International Water Management Institute indicates that solar-powered irrigation can promote sustainable crop farming and boost local food production, decreasing dependence on expensive and unreliable food sources.  The overall objective of this project is to pilot renewable energy-based irrigation systems in three selected communities in the Red Sea State of Sudan. The project also aims to build institutional capacity for the good maintenance and repair of such technologies, throughout training trainers at a selected Technical and Vocational training Institution in the Red Sea State. The results of the pilot will help inform decision of further scale-up to mainstream the technologies through the Kassala State State and beyond.</narrative>
  </description>
